{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/User-Developer Continuity in Blender.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/User-Developer Continuity in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"user developer continuity in blender user developer continuity in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/User-Developer Continuity in Blender.md","fileName":"User-Developer Continuity in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"User-Developer Continuity in Blender","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Python Scripting Environment]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Python Scripting Environment","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/User-Developer Continuity in Blender.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/User-Developer Continuity in Blender.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"user developer continuity in blender user developer continuity in blender","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/User-Developer Continuity in Blender.md","fileName":"User-Developer Continuity in Blender.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"User-Developer Continuity in Blender","heading":"User-Developer Continuity in Blender","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Blender narrows the distance between using a tool and programming it. Many interface actions expose Python operators, the scripting workspace sits beside the modeling interface, and the same data can be changed manually or through `bpy` without translation into a separate application.\n\nThis continuity supports gradual automation. A user can begin with a repeated manual operation, discover its API call, test it, and grow it into a script or add-on. Development becomes an extension of ordinary Blender work rather than a disconnected software project, although robust distribution st